# Iron Linux - core system package list
#
# Kernel, firmware, init system and base APT tooling. This is the minimum
# needed for a bootable, updatable, hardware-capable Debian base. Nothing
# desktop-related lives in this file - see desktop.list.chroot and
# apps.list.chroot.
#
# Format: one binary package name per line. Comments start with '#'.
# live-build installs every *.list.chroot file into the live filesystem
# (which is also what the installer copies to disk), so only put things
# here that make sense both live AND installed.

## --- Kernel ---
linux-image-amd64

## --- CPU microcode ---
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode

## --- Firmware (common Intel/AMD graphics, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, audio DSP) ---
# Debian ships proprietary firmware blobs from the non-free-firmware
# archive area (enabled in auto/config via --archive-areas). Keep this
# list broad enough that a normal laptop/desktop just works, without
# bundling every niche vendor blob (see docs/PACKAGES.md).
firmware-linux
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-sof-signed

## --- Init system / core userspace ---
# Debian's default anyway; listed explicitly so the intent is documented
# and the build doesn't silently depend on debootstrap defaults.
systemd
systemd-sysv
udev
dbus

## --- APT / package management ---
apt
apt-utils
apt-transport-https
ca-certificates
gnupg

## --- Base shell / admin tooling ---
sudo
less
bash-completion
locales
console-setup
keyboard-configuration

## --- Disk / storage utilities (needed live, useful installed) ---
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
parted
gdisk

## --- Basic hardware introspection ---
pciutils
usbutils

## --- Networking basics (NetworkManager itself lives in desktop.list.chroot) ---
iproute2
isc-dhcp-client
openssh-client

## --- Live Bootloaders ---
isolinux
syslinux-common
syslinux-efi
grub-efi-amd64-bin
grub-pc-bin

